0..73 Comment "/// This source states the Hopf family over the 2-sphere: a case into the"
74..133 Comment "/// universe whose arm at the 2-cell is `ua` of a homotopy."
134..137 Comment "///"
138..216 Comment "/// `ua` takes an n-cell of `P ≃ P` at each dimension. At dimension two, the"
217..296 Comment "/// cell is a homotopy of the identity of `P`. Such a map sends each point to a"
297..371 Comment "/// path from the point to itself. The checker reads the cell by its type."
372..445 Comment "/// `ua` of the identity equivalence converts to reflexivity at the type."
446..523 Comment "/// Transport of a point `y` along `ua h` is `h y`, in the checker and in the"
524..535 Comment "/// kernel."
536..539 Comment "///"
540..606 Comment "/// `Path.ap` of the Hopf family on the 2-cell reduces to its arm,"
607..672 Comment "/// `ua selfloop`. Transport of `Base` along that cell is `loop`."
673..676 Comment "///"
677..752 Comment "/// Limits: the image of a cell into the universe is the whole image of one"
753..830 Comment "/// letter along one call. A word of more letters, or an inverse letter, does"
831..846 Comment "/// not reduce."
847..850 Comment "///"
851..901 Comment "/// - see: #6530 — the universe family at a cell"
902..952 Comment "/// - see: #6458 — `Path.ap` of a case on a cell"
953..1024 Comment "/// - see: #6477 — `ua` of the identity equivalence is the empty word"
1025..1105 Comment "/// - see: #6282 — transport along a longer word in a family into the universe"
1106..1156 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere-maps.gandr"
1157..1206 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/univalence.gandr"
